│   │   ├── validate.go         # Validation logic
│   │   └── config_test.go
│   ├── git/
│   │   ├── repository.go       # Git repo detection
│   │   └── repository_test.go
│   ├── parser/
│   │   ├── markdown.go         # Markdown parsing
│   │   ├── writer.go           # Markdown writing
│   │   ├── section.go          # Section handling
│   │   └── parser_test.go
│   ├── project/
│   │   ├── project.go          # Project model
│   │   ├── hierarchy.go        # Hierarchy building
│   │   └── project_test.go
│   ├── todo/
│   │   ├── item.go             # TodoItem model
│   │   ├── operations.go       # CRUD operations
│   │   ├── matcher.go          # Fuzzy matching
│   │   └── todo_test.go
│   └── tui/
│       ├── model.go            # Bubbletea model
│       ├── update.go           # Update handlers
│       ├── view.go             # View rendering
│       ├── components/
│       │   ├── list.go         # List component
│       │   ├── editor.go       # Inline editor
│       │   ├── menu.go         # Menu popup
│       │   └── confirm.go      # Confirmation dialog
│       └── tui_test.go
├── messages/
│   ├── errors.txt              # Error messages
│   ├── help.txt                # Help text
│   └── messages.go             # go:embed loader
├── pkg/                        # Public API (if needed)
├── testdata/
│   ├── configs/                # Test configurations
│   └── markdown/               # Test markdown files
├── .mktodo.yml                 # Project's own config
├── .golangci.yml               # Linter configuration
├── go.mod
├── go.sum
├── main.go                     # Entry point
├── Makefile                    # Build tasks
└── README.md
```

## Implementation Phases

### Phase 0: Project Setup (Week 1)

**Goal:** Establish project foundation with proper tooling and structure.

**Tasks:**

#### 0.1: Initialize Go Module
- [ ] Run `go mod init github.com/jvzantvoort/mktodo`
- [ ] Create basic directory structure
- [ ] Create `main.go` with placeholder
- [ ] Initialize git repository
- [ ] Create `.gitignore` for Go

**Acceptance:**
- Module initialized and importable
- Directory structure matches plan
- Git repository ready

#### 0.2: Configure Development Tools
- [ ] Create `.golangci.yml` with strict rules
- [ ] Create `Makefile` with targets: build, test, lint, clean
- [ ] Set up pre-commit hooks (optional)
- [ ] Document development setup in README

**Acceptance:**
- `make lint` runs golangci-lint successfully
- `make test` runs tests
- `make build` produces binary

#### 0.3: Setup CI/CD Pipeline
- [ ] Create `.github/workflows/ci.yml`
  - Run tests on push/PR
  - Run linters
  - Check code coverage
  - Test on Linux, macOS, Windows
- [ ] Create `.github/workflows/lint.yml`
  - Run golangci-lint
  - Check formatting with gofmt
- [ ] Create `.github/workflows/release.yml`
  - Build binaries for multiple platforms
  - Create GitHub releases

**Acceptance:**
- CI runs on every push
- All checks must pass before merge
- Failed builds block PRs

#### 0.4: Install Dependencies
- [ ] Install Cobra: `go get github.com/spf13/cobra@latest`
- [ ] Install Viper: `go get github.com/spf13/viper@latest`
- [ ] Install Bubbletea: `go get github.com/charmbracelet/bubbletea@latest`
- [ ] Run `go mod tidy`

**Acceptance:**
- All dependencies in `go.mod`
- `go build` succeeds
- No version conflicts

