### Phase 1: Core Foundation (Week 2-3)

**Goal:** Implement basic models, git detection, and configuration loading.

**Tasks:**

#### 1.1: Git Repository Detection
**Priority:** MUST  
**File:** `internal/git/repository.go`

- [ ] Implement `FindGitRoot()` function
  - Traverse parent directories looking for `.git`
  - Return absolute path to git root
  - Return error if not in git repo
- [ ] Write unit tests
- [ ] Add helpful error messages

```go
package git

type Repository struct {
    Root string
}

func FindRepository() (*Repository, error)
func (r *Repository) ConfigPath() string // Returns .mktodo.yml path
```

**Acceptance:**
- Detects git root correctly
- Error message guides user when not in repo
- Tests cover edge cases (root directory, nested repos)

#### 1.2: Configuration Models
**Priority:** MUST  
**File:** `internal/config/config.go`

- [ ] Define `Config` struct
- [ ] Define `ProjectConfig` struct
- [ ] Implement YAML unmarshaling

```go
package config

type Config struct {
    TodoFile string          `yaml:"todofile"`
    Projects []ProjectConfig `yaml:"projects"`
}

type ProjectConfig struct {
    Name   string  `yaml:"name"`
    Title  string  `yaml:"title"`
    Parent *string `yaml:"parent"` // pointer for nil handling
}
```

**Acceptance:**
- Structs unmarshal from YAML correctly
- Handles nil parent values
- Clear struct tags for YAML

#### 1.3: Configuration Loading
**Priority:** MUST  
**File:** `internal/config/config.go`

- [ ] Implement `Load(path string) (*Config, error)`
  - Use Viper to load YAML
  - Unmarshal to Config struct
  - Return errors for missing file
- [ ] Write unit tests with test fixtures
- [ ] Support default values (todofile: README.md)

**Acceptance:**
- Loads valid configurations
- Returns clear errors for invalid YAML
- Tests use `testdata/configs/` fixtures

#### 1.4: Configuration Validation
**Priority:** MUST  
**File:** `internal/config/validate.go`

- [ ] Implement `Validate() error`
  - Check all required fields present
  - Validate parent references exist
  - Detect circular dependencies
  - Validate nesting depth ≤ 6
- [ ] Write comprehensive tests
- [ ] Provide actionable error messages

**Acceptance:**
- Catches all invalid configurations
- Error messages suggest fixes
- Test coverage ≥ 90%

#### 1.5: Project Hierarchy
**Priority:** MUST  
**File:** `internal/project/hierarchy.go`

- [ ] Implement `Project` model
- [ ] Implement `BuildHierarchy(config)` function
  - Create project tree from config
  - Calculate header levels
  - Link parent-child relationships
- [ ] Implement `FindByPath(path string)` for dotted notation
- [ ] Write unit tests

```go
package project

type Project struct {
    Name     string
    Title    string
    Parent   *Project
    Children []*Project
    Level    int
    Items    []*todo.Item
}

func BuildHierarchy(cfg *config.Config) (map[string]*Project, error)
func FindByPath(projects map[string]*Project, path string) (*Project, error)
```

**Acceptance:**
- Correctly builds project tree
- Calculates header levels (1-6)
- Dotted paths resolve correctly (e.g., "lego.technic")
- Test coverage ≥ 85%

