### Phase 2: Markdown Parsing (Week 4-5)

**Goal:** Parse and write markdown files while preserving all non-TODO content.

**Tasks:**

#### 2.1: TODO Item Model
**Priority:** MUST  
**File:** `internal/todo/item.go`

- [ ] Define `Item` struct
- [ ] Implement FIXME detection
- [ ] Implement checkbox parsing

```go
package todo

type Item struct {
    Description string
    Done        bool
    IsFIXME     bool
    LineNumber  int
    Project     *project.Project
}

func Parse(line string) (*Item, error)
func (i *Item) String() string // Format as markdown
```

**Acceptance:**
- Parses all checkbox variations: `- [ ]`, `* [x]`, `+ [X]`
- Detects FIXME prefix (case-insensitive)
- Round-trip: Parse then String returns equivalent

#### 2.2: Markdown Section Parser
**Priority:** MUST  
**File:** `internal/parser/section.go`

- [ ] Define `Section` types (Header, TODO, Other)
- [ ] Implement header level detection
- [ ] Implement section splitting logic

```go
package parser

type SectionType int

const (
    SectionHeader SectionType = iota
    SectionTODO
    SectionOther
)

type Section struct {
    Type    SectionType
    Content string
    Line    int
    Project *project.Project
}

func SplitSections(content string) []Section
```

**Acceptance:**
- Splits markdown into sections correctly
- Preserves exact whitespace and formatting
- Identifies header levels accurately

#### 2.3: Markdown Document Parser
**Priority:** MUST  
**File:** `internal/parser/markdown.go`

- [ ] Implement `Document` struct
- [ ] Implement `Parse(filePath, projects)` function
  - Read markdown file
  - Split into sections
  - Match headers to projects
  - Extract TODO items from sections
- [ ] Preserve all non-TODO content
- [ ] Write comprehensive tests

```go
package parser

type Document struct {
    FilePath string
    Sections []Section
    Projects map[string]*project.Project
}

func Parse(filePath string, projects map[string]*project.Project) (*Document, error)
func (d *Document) FindProject(name string) (*project.Project, error)
```

**Acceptance:**
- Parses complex markdown correctly
- All non-TODO content preserved exactly
- Headers matched to projects
- TODO items extracted with line numbers
- Test coverage ≥ 85%

#### 2.4: Markdown Writer
**Priority:** MUST  
**File:** `internal/parser/writer.go`

- [ ] Implement `Write(filePath string) error`
  - Reconstruct markdown from sections
  - Preserve formatting
  - Use atomic write (temp file + rename)
  - Preserve file permissions
- [ ] Handle line ending preservation (LF/CRLF)
- [ ] Write tests

**Acceptance:**
- Atomic writes (no data loss on failure)
- Permissions preserved
- Line endings preserved
- Round-trip: Parse → Modify → Write → Parse matches
- Test coverage ≥ 80%

