## Appendix A: Development Commands

### Common Tasks
```bash
# Build binary
make build

# Run tests
make test

# Run linter
make lint

# Run all checks (test + lint)
make check

# Generate coverage report
make coverage

# Clean build artifacts
make clean

# Install locally
make install

# Run TUI
./mktodo tui

# Run specific test
go test -v -run TestConfigValidation ./internal/config

# Run benchmarks
go test -bench=. ./internal/parser

# Profile CPU
go test -cpuprofile=cpu.prof -bench=. ./internal/parser

# Profile memory
go test -memprofile=mem.prof -bench=. ./internal/parser
```

### Git Workflow
```bash
# Create feature branch
git checkout -b feature/list-command

# Commit changes
git add .
git commit -m "feat: implement list command"

# Update from develop
git fetch origin
git rebase origin/develop

# Push feature branch
git push -u origin feature/list-command

# Create PR (use GitHub CLI)
gh pr create --title "Add list command" --body "Implements list command with filters"
```

---

## Appendix B: Example .mktodo.yml for Project

The mktodo project will use its own TODO tracking:

```yaml
todofile: README.md
projects:
  - name: default
    title: TODO
    parent: nil
  - name: cli
    title: CLI Development
    parent: nil
  - name: tui
    title: TUI Development
    parent: nil
  - name: testing
    title: Testing
    parent: nil
  - name: docs
    title: Documentation
    parent: nil
```

